course: dictionary
lesson: 10630
title: Unforgiving
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unforgiving has two meanings. About people, it means someone does not forgive others easily and keeps blaming them for wrongs. About places, weather or tasks, it means they are very hard and allow no mistakes.
explain: «The unforgiving servant was forgiven a huge debt but refused to forgive a small debt owed to him.» Here the servant is unforgiving towards another person. He was forgiven, yet he would not forgive someone else, so the clue is the contrast between the two debts.
explain: Use the context to check. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "unwilling to forgive" still fits, so you have the right idea. Words like «unforgiving heat» and «an unforgiving climate» use the second meaning: the conditions are very harsh.
fact: Unforgiving means not forgiving people easily, or very hard and allowing no mistakes.
fact: «Unforgiving» is an adjective: more unforgiving, most unforgiving.
fact: In Bible parables, such as the one about the unforgiving servant, the servant is punished for refusing to forgive.
fact: Many faiths, including Christianity, teach that forgiveness is good.
fact: A desert, a sea or a cliff can be unforgiving, because a small mistake there can be deadly.
exercise: «The unforgiving servant was forgiven a huge debt but refused to forgive a small debt owed to him.» What does unforgiving mean here? | Very rich | Very kind and generous | Lost and confused | *Does not forgive people easily
exercise: Mia says an unforgiving mountain is a friendly, easy climb. What is wrong with her idea? | Mountains cannot have any feelings | Mountains are only found in the sea | *An unforgiving mountain is very hard and allows no mistakes | Mountains are always easy
exercise: Which phrase describes weather that is very harsh? | A gentle breeze | *Unforgiving heat | A soft spring rain | A cosy fire
test: What does «an unforgiving climate» mean? | *A climate that is very harsh and allows no mistakes | A climate that is warm and friendly | A climate that changes every hour | A climate with rain only in winter
test: Why are deserts, seas and cliffs called unforgiving in adventure stories? | They are always quiet and calm | *A small mistake there can be deadly | They are full of fun and games | They appear only in old books
exam: Which sentence uses unforgiving to mean does not forgive people easily? | The cliff path was steep and unforgiving | The desert was unforgiving in the summer sun | *He would not forgive his brother, even after his brother said sorry | The climate here is unforgiving all year round
